WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.602
So why does language sampling matter so much?

00:00:03.682 --> 00:00:07.284
Massively multilingual corpora are wildly imbalanced.

00:00:07.364 --> 00:00:10.966
In the mC4 dataset, English alone has about nine
point seven trillion characters,

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:14.648
more than ninety-two thousand times the data
available for the lowest-resource language,

00:00:14.728 --> 00:00:18.330
Yoruba.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.012
If you train in proportion to the raw data,

00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:25.694
the tail languages barely register at all.

00:00:25.774 --> 00:00:29.376
Deciding how to balance them is an open and
expensive question,

00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:33.058
and the field's default answer, temperature-based
sampling,

00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:36.740
had never actually been evaluated systematically
across model scales.
